You sense the presense of a spoiler -more-


>  What's the difference, in effect, between an artifact and a blessed
>artifact?

Blessed weapons do more damage to undead. I believe they're also less likely
to be stolen by nymphs (succumbi/incubi must ask to remove blessed armor).

>  Same question for bags of holding.  What's the advantage of a blessed bag
>of holding versus a (nonblessed) bag of holding.

Blessed bag of holding confers less weight.

>  How about armor, boots of speed, etc.

See above for armor. There's not much effect for rings or wands. A blessed
luckstone only keeps GOOD luck from timing out. Effect of blessed potions
and scrolls vary. Blessed magic lamps always give a wish. Blessed tinning
kits always produced blessed tins. Blessed magic markers move scrolls one
level "up" the cursed/blessed state (cursed magic markers move them one down).
Blessed scrollbooks can always be memorized. No effect for blessed amulets
(at least in 3.0j).

There may be other advantages that are in 3.1 that aren't in 3.0j. I haven't
done extensive testing though...
